{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "TDzbBkvMRf", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906404, "segment_id": "k0ogByyvcq", "segment_broadcast_id": "TDzbBkvMRf", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Charles Gibson (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906404, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "TDzbBkvMRf", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906404, "segment_id": "ZFqjvbR9gz", "segment_broadcast_id": "TDzbBkvMRf", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Bill / House Vote / Altman Interview", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The House defeat of President Bush's administration's economic rescue plan and the resulting stock market drop reported.  \n\n(Studio: Betsy Stark)  The market reaction to the failure of the bailout bill featured; details given of the sale of Wachovia to Citigroup and the hopes negotiators will hammer out a deal soon.  [Jefferies and Co. chief investment officer Art HOGAN&#134;- comments on the \"stunning shock\"; asserts on the need for the rescue plan.]  [Economic Policy Inst. economist Jared BERNSTEIN&#134;- says we will see how close to the cliff we are.]  [Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON&nbsp- promises to get something done.]  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Report introduced.  \n\n(Capitol Hill: Jake Tapper)  Why the House voted \"no\" to the bailout legislation examined; scenes shown of the vote in the House with the vote by party outlined on screen.  [Representative Patrick KENNEDY&#134;- blames the Republican Party.]  [Representatives John BOEHNER, Paul BROUN&#134;- criticize the proposal.]  [Speaker of the House Nancy PELOSI&nbsp- blames the failed Bush economic policy.]  [Representatives Eric CANTOR&#134;, Barney FRANK&nbsp- offer differing opinions on whether Pelosi's speech is to blame {for the bill's defeat}.]  [President BUSH, PAULSON&nbsp- comment on what's next.]  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson; Washington: George Stephanopoulos)  The surprise over the bill's defeat despite the united leadership, the timetable for what will happen next, how the markets tomorrow will impact the options with the Senate possibly going first to put pressure on the House or open the bill to more negotiations and the impact on presidential politics discussed.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Earlier interview held with Evercore Partners Roger Altman about the House vote and the market reaction.  [ALTMAN&nbsp- comments on the message as to why this bill is necessary for the average Americans; suggests what should be done next now that the credit markets are frozen; predicts the minds of members of Congress will be scared into changing their vote on the bill.] ", "segment_duration": 670, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906405, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "TDzbBkvMRf", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906404, "segment_id": "txs2a5ZIBC", "segmen